1. Definitions

"Opus" means the software, documentation, examples, source code, user
interfaces, MCP tools, schemas, and related files made available in this
repository.

"Licensor" means Smart Crypto Legal S.A.S.

"You" means any individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
license.

"Self-hosted Internal Use" means running Opus on infrastructure controlled by
you or your organization or firm, only for your own legal operations, research,
evaluation, education, development, or internal business workflows. It does not
include operating Opus as a shared, multi-tenant, hosted, managed, resale, or
client-service platform for third parties.

"Commercial Offering" means offering Opus, a modified version of Opus, or a
substantial Opus-powered product or service to third parties for a fee or other
commercial benefit.

"Public Case Tracking Integration" means a connector, adapter, or MCP tool that
performs lawful case-status lookup, docket/proceeding tracking, public court
data normalization, or synchronization using public data or access credentials
lawfully controlled by the self-hoster, without filing, submitting, signing,
paying, or executing legal acts.

2. Grant of Rights

Subject to this license, Licensor grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide,
royalty-free right to:

- read, study, and evaluate the source code;
- copy and run Opus for Self-hosted Internal Use;
- modify Opus for Self-hosted Internal Use;
- develop plugins, integrations, connectors, and contributions;
- develop, run, and contribute Public Case Tracking Integrations for
  Self-hosted Internal Use;
- provide consulting services that help a client run an Opus instance controlled
  by that client, provided you do not operate Opus as a hosted service for
  multiple clients.

3. Restrictions

You may not, without a separate written commercial license from Licensor:

- offer Opus as a hosted or managed service to third parties;
- resell access to Opus, its UI, APIs, MCP tools, or workflows;
- white-label, rebrand, or market Opus as your own competing platform;
- embed Opus as a substantial component of another SaaS, marketplace, workflow
  automation product, legal operations platform, or MCP platform offered to
  third parties;
- operate client data, legal files, judicial credentials, or third-party
  workflows on an Opus instance controlled by you as a service provider;
- offer or enable court filing/radicacion, submission workflows, legal-act
  execution, managed judicial last-mile operations, payment-provider flows, or
  subscription, plan, quota, and commercial-tenant systems as part of a public
  or third-party service;
- remove or obscure copyright, license, fair-code, source-available, or
  trademark notices;
- use the names or marks "Opus SC LegalTech", "SC LegalTech", or related
  logos, product names, or marks except as allowed by TRADEMARKS.md.

4. Closed Modules

This license does not grant any right to closed modules or closed operational
flows not expressly included as public self-hosted functionality in this
repository, including court filing/radicacion or submission connectors,
legal-act execution automations, managed judicial connector operations,
credential vault operations, payment-provider integrations, subscription, plan,
quota, and commercial-tenant systems, monitoring rules, recordings,
screenshots, or production infrastructure used by SC LegalTech.

Public case tracking adapters, public court-information connectors, stubs, and
interfaces may be included so the self-hosted edition can run and so users may
implement their own adapters under their own responsibility.

